.\" -*- coding: UTF-8 -*-
.TH CppDataSet 3 "" "CppDatasetUtil" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
CppDataSet \- recursive Dataset value with optional comments
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <Dataset.h>
.B class Dataset;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Dataset holds null, bool, a signed 64-bit integer, double, string, map or
array. Map and array elements are also Dataset values. Each value may have
its own comments. Maps are sorted by key and arrays preserve their order.
Copying and moving preserve both values and comments.
.SH TYPES AND CONSTRUCTORS
.B Dataset::Map
is std::map<std::string, Dataset>,
.B Dataset::Array
is std::vector<Dataset>, and
.B Dataset::Value
is a std::variant of the supported types. The default constructor creates null
without comments. Constructors also accept nullptr, bool, int, std::int64_t,
double, const char*, std::string, Map and Array. A null const char* throws
std::invalid_argument.
.SH ACCESS
.TP
.B operator[](const std::string& key)
Accesses a map entry. A mutable null value becomes an empty map, and a
missing key is inserted with a null value. The parent value's comments are
preserved. Const access changes nothing and throws std::out_of_range if the
key is missing. Access to a non-map value throws std::logic_error.
.TP
.B operator[](std::size_t index)
Accesses an array element without inserting it. Indices start at zero. A
non-array value throws std::logic_error; an out-of-range index throws
std::out_of_range. Replacing the parent Dataset invalidates references to
its elements.
.TP
.B value() const noexcept
Returns a const reference to Value. On a type mismatch, std::get throws
std::bad_variant_access and std::get_if returns a null pointer.
.SH COMMENTS
.TP
.B comments() const noexcept
Returns a const reference to the comments in their stored order.
.TP
.B set_comments(std::vector<std::string> comments)
Replaces the comments. Specify text without a leading #; embedded line breaks
produce multiple comment lines. YAML and TOML require valid UTF-8 and reject
unsupported control characters and Unicode line separators. TOML comments
that cannot be placed syntactically are omitted. CSV and JSON do not save
comments. Assignment or a successful Load also replaces existing comments.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B Load(const std::string& path)
Loads CSV, JSON, YAML or TOML based on the case-insensitive extension .csv,
\&.json, .yaml, .yml or .toml. Comments are not loaded. Success replaces the
value and comments; failure leaves the Dataset unchanged. I/O errors, invalid
input, and unsupported extensions or values throw std::runtime_error.
.TP
.B "static LoadDirectory(const std::string& path, bool recursive = false)"
Returns a std::list of path and Dataset pairs sorted by path. Subdirectories
are traversed only when recursive=true. Unsupported extensions are ignored.
Symbolic links to files and directories are followed; a target reached by
multiple paths is loaded once per path. Returned paths retain the supplied
directory and link names. A file link's own extension determines its format.
Cycles, broken links, unreadable entries and failed files are skipped with a
warning on stderr. A starting directory that cannot be opened throws
std::runtime_error. Comments are not loaded.
.TP
.B Save(const std::string& path) const
Saves according to the extension. CSV requires an array of nonempty maps
with identical keys and string values; an empty array produces an empty file.
The TOML root must be a map and null is unsupported. Non-finite floating-point
numbers cannot be saved. YAML and TOML save representable comments.
Serialization precedes opening the file, but a write error can leave it
truncated or incomplete. I/O errors, unsupported extensions, and values or
comments that cannot be represented throw std::runtime_error.
.PP
CSV uses the first row as column names and loads each subsequent row as a
map of strings. Duplicate names and inconsistent field counts are errors.
YAML resolves supported core scalars and rejects multiple documents, duplicate
anchors, recursive aliases and unsupported tags. TOML date/time values and
non-finite numbers cannot be loaded.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
#include <Dataset.h>
#include <string>
#include <variant>
Dataset data;
data["server"]["host"] = "localhost";
data["server"]["host"].set_comments({"Server address"});
data.Save("config.yaml");
Dataset loaded;
loaded.Load("config.yaml");
const auto& host = std::get<std::string>(
    loaded["server"]["host"].value());
.fi
.SH DATA-DRIVEN TESTING
Run the following GoogleTest example from the project root. It loads the two
files in Tests/data/nested-values and compares each case's input and expected
host. The file-count and nonempty-case checks help detect skipped data files.
.nf
#include <gtest/gtest.h>
#include "Dataset.h"

TEST(Example, NestedValues) {
  const auto files = Dataset::LoadDirectory("Tests/data/nested-values");
  ASSERT_EQ(files.size(), 2u);
  for (const auto& [path, dataset] : files) {
    SCOPED_TRACE(path);
    const auto& cases = std::get<Dataset::Array>(dataset["cases"].value());
    ASSERT_FALSE(cases.empty());
    for (const auto& item : cases) {
      const Dataset& input = item["input"];
      const Dataset& expected = item["expected"];
      Dataset result;
      result["host"] = std::get<std::string>(input["host"].value());
      EXPECT_EQ(std::get<std::string>(result["host"].value()),
                std::get<std::string>(expected["host"].value()));
    }
  }
}
.fi
